+# Cognitum C15 T3 P2X — exact-input incremental volumetric replay
+
+- Based on the frozen T3 P2W Library checkpoint. Lu, GitHub, original MOT17 data, and the R1 tracking-performance baseline were not modified.
+- New `cognitum/spatial_incremental_volume.py` provides `P2XSession`. A process-local HMAC-protected LRU caches exact-input P2T window outputs, P2S temporal results and complete P2V verification results. The public P2W result is identical to full `advance()`.
+- Explicit internal evaluators were introduced in P2U and P2V; their public `map_scene()` and `analyze()` remain exact full-replay entrypoints, and existing tests still pass.
+- New `proto/cognitum/spatial/v1/incremental_volume.proto` and `cognitum/proto/spatial_incremental_volume_pb2.py` define a typed result/receipt. The HMAC key is ephemeral, never handed to the caller, and not a durable host attestation.
+- Verify: `PYTHONPATH=. python -m pytest -q tests/test_c15_t3_p2x_incremental_volume.py`; `PYTHONPATH=. python tools/verify_protobuf_schemas.py --require`.
+- Profile: `PYTHONPATH=. python tools/run_c15_t3_p2x_profile.py --out /tmp/p2x_profile.json --rounds 5`.
+- Exact full-replay parity can also be demanded for each `P2XSession.advance(req, validate_parity=True)`; that switch deliberately removes most speed benefit.
+- Limitations: cache misses/restarts still trigger full replay, P2U cross-window aggregation still computes fully, upstream source_result construction is excluded from profile, caller-provided sensor/identity statements are unauthenticated, real 3D sensor validation and Windows profiling remain outstanding. No authority to navigate or alter Lu canonical state.
